  "id": "l03",
  "number": 3,
  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Instrumental Case",
  "subtitle": "By means of, with, by · -ena (singular) and -ehi (plural) endings",
  "tags": [
    "New",
    "Cases",
    "Masc. -a nouns"
  ],
  "minutes": 12,
  "revision": {
    "title": "Quick Revision — Lessons I & II",
    "summaryHtml": "You know two cases: <strong>Nominative</strong> (-o/-ā) marks the subject and <strong>Accusative</strong> (-ṃ/-e) marks the object. Together they form: Subject + Object + Verb.",
    "connectionHtml": "<strong>Connection:</strong> The Instrumental adds a <em>third dimension</em> to your sentences. Now you can say by <em>what means</em> an action is done: \"The man goes <em>by chariot</em>.\"",
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "What are the Accusative endings for masc. -a nouns?",
        "a": "<strong>-ṃ</strong> (sg.) / <strong>-e</strong> (pl.)"
      },
      {
        "q": "\"The king goes to the village\" — translate to Pāli.",
        "a": "<strong>Bhūpālo gāmaṃ gacchati</strong>"
      },
      {
        "q": "What does the Accusative case mark?",
        "a": "<strong>The direct object</strong> or <strong>goal of motion</strong>"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "The Instrumental CaseAgent, Means & Accompaniment",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar",
          "html": "The <em>Instrumental</em> Case<br>Agent, Means &amp; Accompaniment"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The Instrumental case expresses the <strong>means or agent</strong> by which an action is done. It translates as <em>\"by,\" \"with,\"</em> or <em>\"by means of.\"</em>"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "html": "Think of it as answering: <strong>By what?</strong> / <strong>With what?</strong> / <strong>Together with whom?</strong>"
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-ena</em> <span>|</span> nara + ena = <em>narena</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-ehi</em> <span>|</span> nara + ehi = <em>narehi</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Cases learned so far — masculine -a nouns",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Function",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nominative",
              "Subject",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-o</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ā</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Accusative",
              "Object",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ṃ</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-e</span>"
            ],
            [
              "Instrumental",
              "By / with",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ena</span>",
              "<span class=\"decl-ending\">-ehi</span>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
